{"id":"[REDACTED]","object":"chat.completion","created":1790942032,"model":"mercury-2","choices":[{"index":0,"message":{"role":"assistant","content":"{\n  \"record_type\": \"reduction\",\n  \"summary\": \"The review examined all 11 target files in the repository. No concrete defects were found in the majority of source fragments. However, three mechanical issues were identified: silent default handling in environment‑variable helpers (flagFromEnv and optionalEnvBoolean) and removal of the Opus fallback in provider‑preflight. Additionally, the diff for adversarial‑review.js renamed the exported function and removed fallback handling, which may affect callers. Fourth‑shape classification added eight explicit throws/gates across adversarial‑review.js and config.js. Several units remain unresolved due to missing provider records or incomplete AST fragments, leaving their defect status indeterminate.\",\n  \"findings\": [\n    {\n      \"description\": \"flagFromEnv silently treats unrecognized environment variable values as false without warning, potentially masking configuration errors.\",\n      \"target\": \"trai_brain/mercury-bridge/adversarial-review.js\",\n      \"status\": \"finding\",\n      \"citations\": [\n        \"trai_brain/mercury-bridge/adversarial-review.js:122-129\"\n      ]\n    },\n    {\n      \"description\": \"optionalEnvBoolean silently returns false for any env value not matching known true/false strings, providing no diagnostic output.\",\n      \"target\": \"trai_brain/mercury-bridge/config.js\",\n      \"status\": \"finding\",\n      \"citations\": [\n        \"trai_brain/mercury-bridge/config.js:81-87\"\n      ]\n    },\n    {\n      \"description\": \"Fallback logic for Opus and Fable challengers was removed, reducing provider coverage and potentially causing pre‑flight failures where Opus would have succeeded.\",\n      \"target\": \"trai_brain/mercury-bridge/provider-preflight.js\",\n      \"status\": \"finding\",\n      \"citations\": [\